summary:
  Unmute-on-volume-change becomes a toggle instead of an absolute 0.

history:
  Raising the volume must unmute; it must never mute a sink that was already
  playing. `toggle` does exactly that every second time. The invariant about
  asking the sink instead of trusting a cached value exists because this area
  has been wrong before.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
    + (p > 0 ? " pactl set-sink-mute @DEFAULT_SINK@ 0 2>/dev/null;" : "")

replace:
    + (p > 0 ? " pactl set-sink-mute @DEFAULT_SINK@ toggle 2>/dev/null;" : "")

expect:
  Nothing today, and that is the finding. The existing mute invariant guards
  toggleSinkMasterMute, where `toggle` is the CORRECT command. This mutant hits
  the VOLUME path, where an absolute 0 is correct and `toggle` mutes every
  second time. Two neighbouring call sites want opposite commands and only one
  of them is guarded.
